{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.PhragmenLindelof","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Asymptotics"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.watson_uniqueness_rhp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.watson_uniqueness_rhp","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonUniqueness.lean#L89-L114","doc":"**Watson uniqueness on the right half-plane.** Two functions analytic on the\nopen right half-plane, continuous on its closure, `O(exp(B‖z‖^c))` with\n`c < 2`, and bounded on the imaginary axis, that agree up to a stretched-\nexponential `≤ C·exp(−b·x^s)` (`b>0`, `s>1`) along the positive real axis,\nare equal on the closed right half-plane. A Borel/Watson wrapper of\n`PhragmenLindelof.eqOn_right_half_plane_of_superexponential_decay`, with the\nsuperexponential hypothesis supplied by `stretchedExp_superpolynomialDecay`.\nThis is the uniqueness half of Watson / Nevanlinna–Sokal, realized. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.stretchedExp_superpolynomialDecay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.stretchedExp_superpolynomialDecay","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonUniqueness.lean#L42-L87","doc":"**Stretched-exponential ⇒ superexponential decay (the `>π`-sector\namplification).** If `‖f x‖ ≤ C·exp(−b·x^s)` eventually with `b > 0` and\n`s > 1`, then `‖f‖` decays superexponentially: `exp(n x)·‖f x‖ → 0` for\nevery `n`. The stretched exponent `s > 1` is precisely what a Watson sector\nof opening `> π` produces, and precisely what upgrades the single-sector\nexponential bound to the strength Phragmén–Lindelöf requires. ","signatureChunk":0}]}